## Monitored domains are more than a list

Push marks the accounts it holds on a monitored domain as your organisation's.
Changing the list changes those accounts as well as the setting:

| What you do | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| Add a domain to `monitored_domains` | Accounts Push already holds on it are marked as your organisation's |
| Remove a domain from `monitored_domains` | Accounts on it are unmarked. **The plan warns and names the domain** |
| Add a domain in the console, while `monitored_domains` is set | The next apply removes it, with the same warning |
| Leave `monitored_domains` out | The provider reads the list and never sends it. The console owns it |
| Remove the resource, or `terraform destroy` | Nothing changes. A warning says Terraform has stopped managing the settings |

The same holds for `monitor_all_domains`: set, it is managed; left out, it is
read and left alone.

Destroy changes nothing because the settings cannot be deleted, and resetting
them would clear the monitored domains and unmark every account on them. To
change them, apply the values you want before removing the resource.

A first apply without an import replaces whatever list the tenant holds, and
its plan shows only your list. The provider reads the tenant during that plan
and warns about every domain the apply would remove, but importing first makes
the plan show the change itself.

